Abstract = {This paper deals with equivariant simultaneous extension of continuous
   maps into linear G-spaces, where G is a compact Lie group. Let Z be a
   metrizable G-space, A a closed invariant subset of Z, and V a locally
   convex linear G-space. Let C(Z, V ) denote the vector space of
   continuous maps from Z into V, and similarly for C(A, V ). We equip
   these mapping spaces with the compact-open topology and the action gf
   defined by (gf)(x) = gf (g-1x). In the paper we construct an equivariant
   simultaneous extension operator from C(A, V ) to C(Z, V ). More
   precisely, there exist an equivariant linear homeomorphic embedding ? :
   C(A, V ) -+ C(Z, V ) and an invariant neighborhood X of A such that
   ?(f)|A = f, Im ?(f) subset of conv (Im f ? \{0\}) and Im (?(f)|X) subset
   of conv (Im f). Moreover, there is an equivariant linear retraction C(Z,
   V ) -+ Im ?. These results fail to be true when G is a compact non-Lie
   group.(c) 2022 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.},
