   (LAGOS), Huatulco, MEXICO, SEP 18-22, 2023},
Abstract = {We investigate the Sidon set problem in the modular case and its
   corresponding version in Ramsey theory. Specifically, we study the
   function (F) over bar (n) that maximizes the size of a Sidon set in
   Z(n), as well as the minimum n such that Z(n) admits no Sidon
   r-partition (a partition whose parts are all Sidon sets), denoted by
   <(SR(r))over bar>, for a fixed positive integer r. We use known results
   and the pigeonhole principle to establish an upper bound of <(SR(r))over
   bar>, which allows us to find the exact values of <(SR(r))over bar> for
   r is an element of \{2, 3, 4, 7\}. We also present a criterion for
   determining the non-existence of almost difference sets (ADS) in Z(n).
   By exploiting such criterion and the connection between ADS sets and the
   existence of Sidon sets in Zn, we derive nontrivial upper bounds of
   <((F(n))over bar> for infinitely many values of n, and we refine the
   upper bound on <(SR(r))over bar>) in multiple cases, determining also
   the exact value for r is an element of \{5, 6\}. Our findings shed new
   light on the behavior of Sidon sets in cyclic groups. In particular, we
   find infinitely many values for which <((F(n))over bar > <((F(n+1))over
   bar>. (C) 2023 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V. This is an open
   access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0)},
